# Testing and Troubleshooting Guide

## Project: Serverless Invoice Scanner

## 1. Testing Objectives

Verify that all AWS services communicate correctly and that invoice processing works from upload to retrieval.

## 2. Functional Testing

| Test ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC01 | User registration | User successfully registers |
| TC02 | User login | Authentication succeeds |
| TC03 | Upload PDF invoice | Invoice uploaded to S3 |
| TC04 | Upload image invoice | Image uploaded to S3 |
| TC05 | S3 event notification | Lambda triggered |
| TC06 | Textract processing | Invoice information extracted |
| TC07 | Bedrock processing | Structured information generated |
| TC08 | DynamoDB storage | Invoice record saved |
| TC09 | Retrieve invoices | Records returned successfully |
| TC10 | Unauthorized API request | Access denied |

## 3. Security Testing

| Test ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| ST01 | Access private S3 bucket | Public access denied |
| ST02 | Access API without authentication | Request rejected |
| ST03 | User accesses another user's invoices | Access denied |
| ST04 | Unauthorized Lambda resource access | Access denied |
| ST05 | Check frontend credentials | No privileged AWS credentials exposed |

## 4. Failure Testing

| Test ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| FT01 | Upload corrupted PDF | Processing fails gracefully |
| FT02 | Upload unsupported file | File rejected |
| FT03 | Textract processing failure | Error logged |
| FT04 | Bedrock invocation failure | Error handled |
| FT05 | DynamoDB write failure | Error logged and handled |
| FT06 | Duplicate processing event | No duplicate invoice record |

## 5. Monitoring

Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor:

- Lambda execution logs.
- Lambda invocation errors.
- Lambda duration.
- API Gateway errors.
- Processing failures.

Use AWS CloudTrail to review API activity and resource changes.

## 6. Troubleshooting Reference

| Problem | Investigation |
|---|---|
| S3 upload failure | Check bucket permissions and presigned URL |
| Lambda not triggered | Check S3 event notification |
| Textract failure | Check IAM permissions and document format |
| Bedrock failure | Check model access and IAM permissions |
| DynamoDB write failure | Check table name and IAM permissions |
| API authorization failure | Check Cognito JWT configuration |
| Frontend connection failure | Check API endpoint and CORS |

## 7. Testing Status

Testing procedures documented.

Actual test results will be recorded after implementation and execution.
